      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk. it just feels like a math problem that doesn't add up. if there's no objective meaning to anything, then life and death are just two different states, right? they both end in nothingness eventually. so why is one considered \"better\" than the other? it feels like choosing to stay is just an arbitrary rule we follow for no reason.",
